/*  Expressions — the precedence ladder of `src/Interpreter/Parser.cs`, rung for rung.

    Loosest first:
        expression     → pipe-expr [ but void is … | but on failure … | or pass the failure off ] [ when … ]
        pipe-expr      → expr-or ( "|" expr-or )*
        expr-or / expr-xor / expr-and / expr-not
        comparison     → joined-to ( = < > <= >= joined-to )*  [ is … ]
        joined-to      → has-check ( joined to addition )*
        has-check      → split-by [ has … ]
        split-by       → text-contains [ split by addition ]
        text-contains  → addition [ contains addition ]
        addition / multiplication / unary
        postfix        → core-primary ( converted to … | trimmed | sorted … | in uppercase … )*
        core-primary   → the rest of the language

    ★ Conditions (`If`, `While`) have a ladder of their own that meets this one at `joined-to`,
    exactly as the C# parser's does.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    // ── Building nodes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `(BinaryExpression left Op right line column)`.
    Bind node to binary, given (the node left, the text op, the node right, the token spot-tok):
        Return cast made on ("BinaryExpression", a series with (
            left, cast atom on (op), right, cast row-of on (spot-tok), cast column-of on (spot-tok))).
    Done.

    Bind node to unary, given (the text op, the node operand, the token spot-tok):
        Return cast made on ("UnaryExpression", a series with (
            cast atom on (op), operand, cast row-of on (spot-tok), cast column-of on (spot-tok))).
    Done.

    Bind node to variable-named, given (the text name, the token spot-tok):
        Return cast placed on ("VariableReference", a series with (cast quoted on (name)), spot-tok).
    Done.

    // ── The expression ladder ─────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind node or failure to expression unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's pipe-expr or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.

        If cast one's peek-kind is "But":
            Define but-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "On":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Failure") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define fallback as cast one's expr-or or pass the failure off.
                Return cast one's when-suffix on (cast placed on ("FailureFallback", a series with (left, fallback), but-tok))
                    or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Cast one's consume on ("Void") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Is") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define fallback as cast one's expr-or or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's when-suffix on (cast placed on ("ButVoidDefault", a series with (left, fallback), but-tok))
                or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        If cast one's peek-kind is "Or" and cast one's kind-after is "Pass":
            Define or-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Pass") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Failure") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Off") or pass the failure off.
            Return cast one's when-suffix on (cast placed on ("FailurePropagate", a series with (left), or-tok))
                or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        Return cast one's when-suffix on (left) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `<value> when <condition>, otherwise <alternative>` — right-associative.
    Bind node or failure to when-suffix unto parser, given (the node left):
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "When", return left.
        Define when-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define condition as cast one's expr-or or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Comma") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("Otherwise") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define alternative as cast one's expression or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("ConditionalExpression", a series with (left, condition, alternative), when-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to pipe-expr unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's expr-or or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Pipe", repeat:
            Define pipe-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's expr-or or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast placed on ("PipeExpression", a series with (left, right), pipe-tok).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to expr-or unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's expr-xor or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Or" and cast one's kind-after is not "Pass", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's expr-xor or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, "Or", right, op-tok).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to expr-xor unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's expr-and or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Xor", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's expr-and or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, "Xor", right, op-tok).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to expr-and unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's expr-not or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "And", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's expr-not or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, "And", right, op-tok).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to expr-not unto parser:
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Not":
            Define not-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define operand as cast one's expr-not or pass the failure off.
            Return cast unary on ("Not", operand, not-tok).
        Done.
        Return cast one's comparison or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-symbol-comparison, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "Equal" or kind is "Lt" or kind is "Gt" or kind is "Lte" or kind is "Gte".
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to comparison unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
        While cast is-symbol-comparison on (cast one's peek-kind), repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, op-tok's kind, right, op-tok).
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Is":
            Define is-tok as cast one's advance.
            Return cast one's after-is on (left, is-tok) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    /// IsTypeTestArticle — `a` or `an`, never `the`.
    Bind fact to is-type-test-article, given (the token candidate):
        If candidate's kind is not "Article", return false.
        Return cast spelled on (candidate, "a") or cast spelled on (candidate, "an").
    Done.

    /// Everything after an `is` — a type test, or a word comparison. Shared by the expression and
    /// the condition ladders, which ask the same questions in the same order.
    Bind node or failure to after-is unto parser, given (the node left, the token is-tok):
        If cast is-type-test-article on (cast one's peek):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define tested as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("IsTypeCheck", a series with (left, tested, cast flag on (false)), is-tok).
        Done.
        Define following as cast one's token-at on (one's at + 1).
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Not" and cast is-type-test-article on (following):
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define tested as cast one's type-annotation or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("IsTypeCheck", a series with (left, tested, cast flag on (true)), is-tok).
        Done.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Return cast one's word-comparison on (left, is-tok) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to word-comparison unto parser, given (the node left, the token is-tok):
        Define kind as cast one's peek-kind.
        If kind is "Not":
            Define not-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Greater":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Than") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define right as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
                Return cast binary on (left, "Lte", right, not-tok).
            Done.
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Less":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("Than") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define right as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
                Return cast binary on (left, "Gte", right, not-tok).
            Done.
            Define following as cast one's token-at on (one's at + 1).
            If cast one's peek-kind is "Identifier" and cast one's is-word on ("equal") and following's kind is "To":
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
            Done.
            Define right as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
            Return cast binary on (left, "NotEqual", right, not-tok).
        Done.
        If kind is "Greater" or kind is "Less":
            Define word-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("Than") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
            Define op as "Gt" when kind is "Greater", otherwise "Lt".
            Return cast binary on (left, op, right, word-tok).
        Done.
        If kind is "More":
            Define more-tok as cast one's advance.
            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (more-tok,
                "'is more than' isn't a comparison Cufet recognises — did you mean 'is greater than'? "
                joined to "For example: 'While count is greater than 0, repeat:'.")).
        Done.
        Define right as cast one's joined-to or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define beyond as cast one's kind-after.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Or" and (beyond is "More" or beyond is "Less"):
            Cast one's consume on ("Or") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define tail as cast one's advance.
            Define op as "Gte" when tail's kind is "More", otherwise "Lte".
            Return cast binary on (left, op, right, is-tok).
        Done.
        Return cast binary on (left, "Equal", right, is-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to has-check unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's split-by or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "Has", return left.
        Define has-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define shape as cast one's effective-kind on (cast one's peek).
        If shape is not "Entry" and shape is not "Key":
            Define member as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
            Return cast placed on ("SetHasMember", a series with (left, member), has-tok).
        Done.
        Cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("For") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define key as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
        Define kind as "MapHasEntry" when shape is "Entry", otherwise "MapHasKey".
        Return cast placed on (kind, a series with (left, key), has-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to split-by unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's text-contains or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "Split", return left.
        Define split-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Cast one's consume on ("By") or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define delimiter as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("TextSplit", a series with (left, delimiter), split-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to text-contains unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        // `<text> starts with <affix>` / `ends with` — contextual: a plain word with `with` right after.
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Identifier" and cast one's kind-after is "With":
            If cast one's is-word on ("starts") or cast one's is-word on ("ends"):
                Define edge-tok as cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("With") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define affix as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
                Return cast placed on ("TextAffixTest", a series with (left, affix,
                    cast flag on ((edge-tok's lexeme in lowercase) is "ends")), edge-tok).
            Done.
        Done.
        If cast one's peek-kind is not "Contains", return left.
        Define contains-tok as cast one's advance.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Define part as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
        Return cast placed on ("TextContains", a series with (left, part), contains-tok).
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to joined-to unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's has-check or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Joined", repeat:
            Define joined-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's addition or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast placed on ("TextJoin", a series with (left, right), joined-tok).
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to addition unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's multiplication or pass the failure off.
        While cast one's peek-kind is "Plus" or cast one's peek-kind is "Minus", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's multiplication or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, op-tok's kind, right, op-tok).
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to multiplication unto parser:
        Define left as cast one's unary-expr or pass the failure off.
        Define kind as cast one's peek-kind.
        While kind is "Star" or kind is "Slash" or kind is "Percent", repeat:
            Define op-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define right as cast one's unary-expr or pass the failure off.
            The left becomes cast binary on (left, op-tok's kind, right, op-tok).
            The kind becomes cast one's peek-kind.
        Done.
        Return left.
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to unary-expr unto parser:
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Minus":
            Define minus-tok as cast one's advance.
            Define operand as cast one's unary-expr or pass the failure off.
            Return cast unary on ("Minus", operand, minus-tok).
        Done.
        Return cast one's postfix or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// ParseNegation — a minus, then a primary with NO postfix: `math's floor of x converted to
    /// text` converts the floor, not the x.
    Bind node or failure to negation unto parser:
        If cast one's peek-kind is "Minus":
            Define minus-tok as cast one's advance.
            Define operand as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
            Return cast unary on ("Minus", operand, minus-tok).
        Done.
        Return cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    // ── Postfix ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind text to bits-base-for, given (the text lexeme):
        Define lowered as lexeme in lowercase.
        If lowered is "hex", return "x".
        If lowered is "binary", return "b".
        If lowered is "octal", return "o".
        Return "".
    Done.

    Bind node or failure to postfix unto parser:
        Define base as cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.

        While cast one's peek-kind is "Converted", repeat:
            Define converted-tok as cast one's advance.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Cast one's consume on ("To") or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
            Define target as cast one's peek.
            If target's kind is "NumberKw":
                Cast one's advance.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("NumberConvert", a series with (base), converted-tok).
            Done.
            Otherwise if target's kind is "Identifier" and cast spelled on (target, "text"):
                Cast one's advance.
                Define conversion as cast placed on ("TextConvert", a series with (base), converted-tok).
                Cast conversion's add on (cast flag on (false)).
                The base becomes conversion.
            Done.
            Otherwise if target's kind is "Identifier" and cast bits-base-for on (target's lexeme) is not "":
                Cast one's advance.
                The base becomes cast made on ("BitsConvert", a series with (base,
                    cast quoted on (cast bits-base-for on (target's lexeme)),
                    cast row-of on (converted-tok), cast column-of on (converted-tok))).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Return a failure (cast one's expecting on (target,
                    "text, number, hex, binary or octal — expected after 'converted to'")).
            Done.
            Cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.

        Define scanning as true.
        While scanning, repeat:
            Define kind as cast one's peek-kind.
            Define following as cast one's kind-after.
            If cast one's is-word on ("at"):
                Define at-tok as cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define width as cast one's unary-expr or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                If cast one's is-word on ("bits") is false:
                    Return a failure (cast one's refused on (cast one's peek,
                        "expected 'bits' after a stated width — the phrase is '<value> at <n> bits', as in '0b0 at 3 bits'.")).
                Done.
                Cast one's advance.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("BitsAtWidth", a series with (base, width), at-tok).
                Skip.
            Done.
            If kind is "Shifted":
                Define shifted-tok as cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define direction as cast one's peek.
                Define leftward as direction's kind is "Identifier" and cast spelled on (direction, "left").
                Define rightward as direction's kind is "Identifier" and cast spelled on (direction, "right").
                If leftward is false and rightward is false:
                    Return a failure (cast one's refused on (direction, "expected 'left' or 'right' after 'shifted'")).
                Done.
                Cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Cast one's consume on ("By") or pass the failure off.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define amount as cast one's unary-expr or pass the failure off.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("BitsShift", a series with (base, cast flag on (leftward), amount), shifted-tok).
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Skip.
            Done.
            If kind is "Sorted":
                Define sorted-tok as cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define by-field as cast nothing.
                Define by-lambda as cast nothing.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "By":
                    Cast one's advance.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    If cast one's peek-kind is "FunctionKw":
                        Define key-tok as cast one's peek.
                        The by-lambda becomes cast one's core-primary or pass the failure off.
                        If by-lambda's kind is not "LambdaLiteral":
                            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (key-tok, "expected a function literal after 'sorted by'")).
                        Done.
                    Done.
                    Otherwise:
                        Define field-tok as cast one's consume on ("Identifier") or pass the failure off.
                        The by-field becomes cast quoted on (field-tok's lexeme).
                    Done.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                Done.
                Define reversed as false.
                If cast one's peek-kind is "In" and cast one's kind-after is "Reverse":
                    Cast one's advance.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                    Cast one's advance.
                    The reversed becomes true.
                    Cast one's skip-noise.
                Done.
                The base becomes cast made on ("SortExpression", a series with (base, by-field,
                    cast flag on (reversed), cast row-of on (sorted-tok), cast column-of on (sorted-tok), by-lambda)).
            Done.
            Otherwise if kind is "Trimmed":
                Define trimmed-tok as cast one's advance.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("TextTrim", a series with (base), trimmed-tok).
            Done.
            Otherwise if kind is "In" and (following is "Uppercase" or following is "Lowercase"):
                Define in-tok as cast one's advance.
                Cast one's skip-noise.
                Define upper as cast one's peek-kind is "Uppercase".
                Cast one's advance.
                The base becomes cast placed on ("TextCase", a series with (base, cast flag on (upper)), in-tok).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The scanning becomes false.
            Done.
            If scanning, cast one's skip-noise.
        Done.

        Return base.
    Done.
Done.
